# Environment for the hub chat gateway (EnvironmentFile of the user unit agent-hub-gateway.service). Placeholders only.
# Keep this file in the gateway directory below (mode 0600), never in the socket directory: the socket directory is
# mounted into the hub container.
# Absolute path of the orchestrator workspace: the working directory of every web run.
WORKSPACE_DIR=/path/to/orchestrator-workspace
# The gateway's own directory (mode 0700, not mounted anywhere): audit log and the kill-switch file live here.
GATEWAY_DATA_DIR=/path/to/hub-gateway
# The socket lives in its own directory (mode 0700), the only one the hub container mounts (read-only). The path
# must be 100 bytes or shorter. The file name must match GATEWAY_SOCKET in the app's compose file (gateway.sock).
GATEWAY_SOCKET=/path/to/hub-socket/gateway.sock
# Optional overrides (defaults shown).
# KILL_SWITCH_FILE=/path/to/hub-gateway/DISABLED
# AUDIT_LOG=/path/to/hub-gateway/audit.log
# CLAUDE_BIN=/path/to/claude          absolute path recommended: a service has a short PATH
# PATH=/path/to/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin   what the claude process (and its hooks) will see
# GATEWAY_MODEL=
# RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
# MAX_OUT_BYTES=8388608
# KILL_GRACE_MS=3000
# EXIT_GRACE_MS=2000       a run is finished this long after its process exits, even if a stray process holds the pipe
# KILL_POLL_MS=1000        how often a run in progress checks the kill switch
# GATEWAY_DISABLED=0       1 turns every web run off (the file flag above does the same without a restart)
